  "basis": "Reviewed BMA150 factory defaults, staggered T/X/Y/Z acquisition, signed moving-average history, temperature and Bosch-derived offset scale. Additional sensor appointments exposed watch ticks dropped at oscillator-stabilization completion; the transition now synchronizes the old interval before changing gates. An isolated unchanged-data sensor experiment at 3 kHz versus 12 kHz now produces identical 10-second CPU, RAM, display, and persistent exports. The independent 8448-us watch-edge fixture fails before the fix (33 ticks) and passes after it (34). All four retail workloads and partition/snapshot replay pass without faults, resets, or persistent writes. The ADC board revision replaces the fixed 3.3 V scaffold with supply-following AVCC and a P84-switched effective 600 mV drop; only initial condition metadata changes, with all execution and export expectations retained. These are software regression observations, not hardware measurements. The exception-stack correction duplicates CCR in both bytes, as the target stack diagram and inherited H8/300 format specify. The idle RAM export changes only FF69 from 00 to 08, matching CCR at FF68; every other export and execution expectation remains unchanged. The analog-stage patch based on this revision adds the Bosch-documented second-order 1500-Hz pre-ADC response with chosen Butterworth damping. Independent step, frequency-sweep and between-conversion pulse tests distinguish its behavior; the pulse guest fails with the previous direct-sampling model and passes with the filter. Reviewed walking changes are two fewer retired instructions, eight additional bus reads and twelve RAM bytes in F7E6..F850. RuntimeState, final CPU registers, interrupt/event/serial totals, LCD/frame and all persistent exports remain unchanged; home, menu and idle expectations are identical. See docs/research/bma150-analog-implementation.md for the model and comparison receipts.",
  "change_policy": "Review independent hardware evidence before rebasing an expectation. The verifier never updates this file.",
